<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "virtual-instrument compatibility statement"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#IdentifiedResource> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A qualified, evidence-backed statement about the compatibility of a virtual-instrument version with a host, platform, protocol, plugin format, or operating environment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A compatibility statement applies only to the named version and target under the conditions supported by its evidence. It is not a certification or a guarantee for other versions, environments, or future states."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "virtual-instrument source relation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#IdentifiedResource> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A qualified and evidence-backed relation connecting a virtual instrument, product, or version to a specific musical instrument or instrument state used as a sample source, model, reconstruction target, composite source, or inspiration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#InstrumentSourceRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A source relation does not assert that the virtual and source instruments are identical. Ambiguous candidates remain assertions or review proposals rather than accepted source relations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "virtual-instrument package"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/media#DigitalAsset> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An installable, downloadable, or preservable digital asset distributing all or part of a virtual-instrument version."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentPackage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A package is not automatically the playable instrument; it may require a host, engine, dependency, license, configuration, or additional package."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "virtual-instrument product"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A stable product, library, sample-set, plugin, or project identity under which one or more virtual-instrument versions are developed or distributed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A product may realize one playable virtual musical instrument or contain several instruments. Product identity is not automatically musical-instrument identity; generic hosts and dependencies that implement no playable instrument are outside this class."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "virtual-instrument version"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualInstrumentVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A versioned edition or release state of a virtual-instrument product, distinct from both the stable product identity and its downloadable packages."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "virtual musical instrument"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A musical instrument whose playable sound-producing or control behavior is realized substantially through software, digital computation, or a software-controlled sample or synthesis system."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#VirtualMusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This class identifies the playable instrument, not merely a catalog row, download page, package, sample library component, or representation of a physical instrument."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#CompatibilityStatement> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "compatibility status"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Classifies the result of a compatibility statement with a governed status concept."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Indeterminate means that the available evidence supports neither a positive nor a negative result; it must not be interpreted as compatible-with-limitations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityTarget> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/virtual-instrument#compatibilityTarget> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
